From: QVAC SDK Pod <noreply@tether.io>
Subject: [PATCH] chatterbox: propagate s3gen_preload failures from Engine::Impl::Impl

s3gen_preload() catches std::exception, logs to stderr, and returns 1 on
failure (chatterbox_tts.cpp:2944-2952). The Engine::Impl constructor's
preload thread (chatterbox_engine.cpp:181-184) discards that return
value and joins the thread without checking, so an out-of-memory failure
from ggml_backend_alloc_ctx_tensors leaves the global s3gen cache empty
while the constructor returns "successfully".

The first synthesize() call then re-enters s3gen_model_cache_get, gets a
cache miss, retries load_s3gen_gguf, and re-throws the same OOM. From
the SDK consumer's perspective this looks like a synthesize-time failure
("engine.synthesize: load_s3gen_gguf: ggml_backend_alloc_ctx_tensors
failed for s3gen weights buffer"), even though the engine was
constructed-but-broken from the start. Worse, the stderr log from
s3gen_preload is invisible on iOS (Bare runtime) so the real cause is
lost.

Capture a std::exception_ptr in the preload thread when s3gen_preload
returns nonzero, then rethrow from the constructor after
wait_for_preload(). Mirrors the existing bake_voice_conditioning()
failure-cleanup style: free the gallocr and the partially-loaded model
before throwing. The resource manager / SDK loader treats this as a
clean loadModel failure (instead of caching a zombie engine), and the
test report accurately attributes the failure to the load step.

Pairs with the prior NULL-guard / NULL-check fixes in ggml-speech and
tts-cpp's load_s3gen_gguf -- those convert the SIGSEGV/SIGABRT into a
clean std::runtime_error; this patch makes sure that error is reported
at the right callsite (loadModel, not synthesize).

---
 tts-cpp/src/chatterbox_engine.cpp | 22 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tts-cpp/src/chatterbox_engine.cpp b/tts-cpp/src/chatterbox_engine.cpp
--- a/tts-cpp/src/chatterbox_engine.cpp
+++ b/tts-cpp/src/chatterbox_engine.cpp
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 
 #include <atomic>
 #include <chrono>
+#include <exception>
 #include <cstring>
 #include <filesystem>
 #include <stdexcept>
@@ -42,6 +43,11 @@ struct Engine::Impl {
     chatterbox_model     model{};
     ggml_gallocr_t       allocr = nullptr;
     std::thread          s3gen_preload_thread;
+    // Set by the s3gen preload thread when s3gen_preload() returns
+    // non-zero (which silently swallows the underlying std::exception
+    // from s3gen_model_cache_get / load_s3gen_gguf). Read by the Impl
+    // constructor after wait_for_preload() to decide whether to throw.
+    std::exception_ptr   s3gen_preload_err;
 
     // Baked voice-conditioning state.  Populated at construction when
     // `reference_audio` or `voice_dir` is set, then reused by every
@@ -178,9 +184,14 @@ struct Engine::Impl {
             throw;
         }
 
-        s3gen_preload_thread = std::thread([path = opts.s3gen_gguf_path,
+        s3gen_preload_thread = std::thread([this,
+                                            path = opts.s3gen_gguf_path,
                                             ngpu = opts.n_gpu_layers]() {
-            s3gen_preload(path, ngpu);
+            if (s3gen_preload(path, ngpu) != 0) {
+                s3gen_preload_err = std::make_exception_ptr(std::runtime_error(
+                    "Engine: s3gen weights preload failed for " + path +
+                    " (backend out of memory? see earlier stderr for details)"));
+            }
         });
 
         // Block until s3gen_preload finishes its Metal buffer allocation
@@ -197,6 +208,16 @@ struct Engine::Impl {
         // ggml-metal's shared buffer-type init is safe to use from a
         // preload thread concurrent with construction-time teardown.
         wait_for_preload(s3gen_preload_thread);
+
+        // If the preload thread captured an exception (s3gen_preload
+        // returned 1 -- the original throw was swallowed and stderr-logged
+        // by s3gen_preload itself), surface it as a clean construction
+        // failure rather than leaving the engine in a half-loaded state.
+        if (s3gen_preload_err) {
+            if (allocr) { ggml_gallocr_free(allocr); allocr = nullptr; }
+            free_model();
+            std::rethrow_exception(s3gen_preload_err);
+        }
     }
 
     ~Impl() {
